:false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":486108,"name":"","username":"krstoevan","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/k/3ec8ea/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T08:39:53.631Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003ebtw, i dont code… no.. i dont code w cursor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eso cursor pro is not useful to me, at all.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ethanks\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T08:39:53.631Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":1.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171010,"topic_slug":"i-m-on-supergrok-and-want-to-buy-additional-grok-bot-requests-but-on-demand-billing-appears-to-require-a-cursor-pro-subscription","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":9826,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/i-m-on-supergrok-and-want-to-buy-additional-grok-bot-requests-but-on-demand-billing-appears-to-require-a-cursor-pro-subscription/171010/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486117,"name":"","username":"krstoevan","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/k/3ec8ea/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T08:43:05.224Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eGPT, after digging w CDP/CDT on chrome on this fourm:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes—there’s already a fairly clear answer in related Cursor forum threads:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLinking SuperGrok grants Grok Bot access and its included weekly allowance, but it does not create or upgrade a Cursor plan. \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/did-i-miss-an-announcement-on-supergrok-heavy-and-cursor-ultra/169128/13\"\u003eCursor Billing’s response\u003c/a\u003e confirms this.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOnce the weekly Grok Bot allowance is exhausted, extra usage can use Cursor’s shared On‑Demand pool—but only if On‑Demand is enabled on the Cursor account. \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/help/grok-bot/plans\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCurrent Cursor docs\u003c/a\u003e state that the SuperGrok link “does not change your Cursor plan.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTherefore, your observation is likely correct: a SuperGrok-only account remains Cursor Free, and Cursor requires a paid plan such as Pro before enabling On‑Demand. The forum reports describe the same “Cursor Free → buy Pro” behavior. \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/is-supergrok-heavy-now-the-better-cursor-ultra-deal/168558/62\"\u003eRelated forum discussion\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI couldn’t verify whether your newly created thread already has a reply—the live page wasn’t accessible through the browser connection—but the existing answer is: SuperGrok gives you the weekly Grok Bot allowance, not a standalone paid Cursor billing relationship or an On‑Demand wallet.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T08:43:05.224Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":1.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171010,"topic_slug":"i-m-on-supergrok-and-want-to-buy-additional-grok-bot-requests-but-on-demand-billing-appears-to-require-a-cursor-pro-subscription","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/is-supergrok-heavy-now-the-better-cursor-ultra-deal/168558/62","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Is SuperGrok Heavy now the better Cursor Ultra deal?","clicks":1},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/did-i-miss-an-announcement-on-supergrok-heavy-and-cursor-ultra/169128/13","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Did I miss an announcement on SuperGrok Heavy and Cursor Ultra?","clicks":0},{"url":"https://cursor.com/help/grok-bot/plans","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Plans and billing | Cursor Docs","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":9826,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/i-m-on-supergrok-and-want-to-buy-additional-grok-bot-requests-but-on-demand-billing-appears-to-require-a-cursor-pro-subscription/171010/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":487897,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T06:17:33.006Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report. You don’t need Cursor Pro for this, and it’s definitely not worth buying Pro just for Grok Bot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe key point is that Pro and SuperGrok pools don’t stack. Even if you buy Pro, it won’t add any Grok Bot usage. So it can’t solve “I want more Grok Bot” at all. Don’t buy it for that.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow to get more usage the right way:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA SuperGrok subscription linked to your Cursor account gives you a weekly Grok Bot allowance. This is a usage grant, it does not create a paid Cursor plan. You can stay on Free and that’s fine.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen the weekly amount runs out, the correct way to get extra usage is on-demand usage on the same account with an active SuperGrok link. It’ll ask you to add a card.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe “Pro required” message usually shows up when the account you’re viewing doesn’t have SuperGrok linked. For example, you’re on a free trial credit, or you’re logged into \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e with a different account than the one Grok Bot is using.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot → Settings → plan / usage screen. Check which email is signed in and whether it shows SuperGrok as the plan.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf SuperGrok isn’t shown there, link the subscription via Get Access with Grok, or open \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/promos/super-grok\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCursor - The best way to code with AI\u003c/a\u003e while logged into \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e with the same account. The link is permanent, so use the account you plan to keep using with Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOnce the account shows an active SuperGrok link, open \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/dashboard/spending\"\u003ehttps://cursor.com/dashboard/spending\u003c/a\u003e on the same account, find On-Demand Usage, and enable it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGo back to Grok Bot and send a message. It should work even after the weekly amount is used up.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne more note. SuperGrok Lite does not include Grok Bot. Grok Bot comes with SuperGrok, SuperGrok Plus, SuperGrok Heavy, and X Premium+. Based on your description SuperGrok India, you likely have base SuperGrok, which supports Grok Bot and on-demand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf after step 3, with an active SuperGrok link, the spending page still asks for a paid Cursor plan, send the email shown in Grok Bot and a screenshot of that page and I’ll take a look. Either way, buying Pro won’t fix your issue, so start with linking and on-demand.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T06:17:33.006Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":21.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171010,"topic_slug":"i-m-on-supergrok-and-want-to-buy-additional-grok-bot-requests-but-on-demand-billing-appears-to-require-a-cursor-pro-subscription","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com/promos/super-grok","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Cursor - The best way to code with AI","clicks":0},{"url":"https://cursor.com/dashboard/spending","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0},{"url":"http://cursor.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"AI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/i-m-on-supergrok-and-want-to-buy-additional-grok-bot-requests-but-on-demand-billing-appear